{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for the details. Your temporary password is working. You get as far as the change-password screen, and your account isn't locked. The error almost always means the new password doesn't meet our rules or the change was made from the wrong place. Please try this:\n\n1. Sign in on your laptop's Windows sign-in screen, not a web page. Your laptop needs to be connected to the office network, or to the VPN if you're at home.\n2. Make your new password at least 14 characters long. It can't be the same as a recent password. A short phrase of a few words works well.\n3. Make sure Caps Lock is off and the keyboard language is right. Watch for letters and numbers that look alike, like l and I, or 0 and O.\n\nIf it still fails, please reply and tell us: (a) whether you were on the Windows sign-in screen or a web page, (b) whether you were in the office or at home, and (c) the exact wording of the error. Please don't send any passwords. If too many tries lock your account, tell us and we'll unlock it.",
  "internal_note": "KB-003 checks: user_id 12 is active, must_change_password=true, failed_login_count=0, not locked, sign-in not blocked, VPN access enabled. password_last_set 2026-10-11 02:57 UTC (temp password issued at onboarding). Sign-in logs for the last 14 days: all successful, from NY corporate or residential networks during work hours, 0 failed attempts, no hosting networks. Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Win11) is online with no warnings. The temporary password is accepted, so the failure happens at the change step. Likely causes: the new password breaks policy (14+ chars, no reuse), or the change is being made on a web page or off-network instead of the Windows sign-in screen on corp/VPN. Sent the user the KB-003 fix steps and asked where she makes the change and for the exact error text. No actions queued. If the account locks, queue unlock_account. If it still fails with a policy-compliant password on the sign-in screen while on corp/VPN, issue a new temp password per KB-002 or escalate.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-003",
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
